es":{"alchemy":"not_legal","brawl":"not_legal","commander":"legal","competitivebrawl":"not_legal","duel":"legal","future":"not_legal","gladiator":"not_legal","historic":"not_legal","legacy":"legal","modern":"legal","oathbreaker":"legal","oldschool":"not_legal","pauper":"legal","paupercommander":"legal","penny":"not_legal","pioneer":"not_legal","predh":"legal","premodern":"not_legal","standard":"not_legal","standardbrawl":"not_legal","timeless":"not_legal","tlr":"legal","vintage":"legal"},"loyalty":null,"mana_cost":"{G}","name":"Viridescent Wisps","oracle_id":"3003e19e-ae60-4e10-b688-d0cac2a63cb2","oracle_text":"Target creature becomes green and gets +1/+0 until end of turn.\nDraw a card.","power":null,"produced_mana":[],"released_at":"2008-05-02","toughness":null,"type_line":"Instant"},{"cmc":2.0,"color_identity":["B"],"colors":["B"],"defense":null,"keywords":[],"layout":"normal","legalities":{"alchemy":"not_legal","brawl":"legal","commander":"legal","competitivebrawl":"legal","duel":"legal","future":"not_legal","gladiator":"legal","historic":"legal","legacy":"legal","modern":"legal","oathbreaker":"legal","oldschool":"not_legal","pauper":"legal","paupercommander":"legal","penny":"legal","pioneer":"legal","predh":"not_legal","premodern":"not_legal","standard":"not_legal","standardbrawl":"not_legal","timeless":"legal","tlr":"legal","vintage":"legal"},"loyalty":null,"mana_cost":"{1}{B}","name":"Walking Corpse","oracle_id":"fea95888-e16a-4209-9cd4-623f7f4d2f67","oracle_text":"","power":"2","produced_mana":[],"released_at":"2020-07-03","toughness":"2","type_line":"Creature — Zombie"},{"cmc":0.0,"color_identity":[],"colors":[],"defense":null,"keywords":[],"layout":"normal","legalities":{"alchemy":"legal","brawl":"legal","commander":"legal","competitivebrawl":"legal","duel":"legal","future":"legal","gladiator":"legal","historic":"legal","legacy":"legal","modern":"legal","oathbreaker":"legal","oldschool":"not_legal","pauper":"legal","paupercommander":"legal","penny":"not_legal","pioneer":"legal","predh":"not_legal","premodern":"not_legal","standard":"legal","standardbrawl":"legal","timeless":"legal","tlr":"legal","vintage":"legal"},"loyalty":null,"mana_cost":"","name":"Wastes","oracle_id":"05d24b0c-904a-46b6-b42a-96a4d91a0dd4","oracle_text":"{T}: Add {C}.","power":null,"produced_mana":["C"],"released_at":"2025-08-01","toughness":null,"type_line":"Basic Land"}],"fixture_kind":"public_exact-list_card_data","rulings":[{"comment":"Because Wastes is a basic land, you can include as many of them as you like in your Constructed decks.","oracle_id":"05d24b0c-904a-46b6-b42a-96a4d91a0dd4","published_at":"2021-03-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"In Limited events (including Sealed Deck and Booster Draft), Wastes must be in your card pool to be included in your deck. You can't add Wastes to your card pool in the same way that you can add other basic lands.","oracle_id":"05d24b0c-904a-46b6-b42a-96a4d91a0dd4","published_at":"2021-03-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Wastes is not a land type. If something asks you to name a land type, you can't choose Wastes.","oracle_id":"05d24b0c-904a-46b6-b42a-96a4d91a0dd4","published_at":"2021-03-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"An effect that changes a permanent’s colors overwrites all its old colors unless it specifically says “in addition to its other colors.” For example, after Cerulean Wisps resolves, the affected creature will just be blue. It doesn’t matter what colors it used to be (even if, for example, it used to be blue and black).","oracle_id":"3003e19e-ae60-4e10-b688-d0cac2a63cb2","published_at":"2008-05-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Changing a permanent’s color won’t change its text. If you turn Wilt-Leaf Liege blue, it will still affect green creatures and white creatures.","oracle_id":"3003e19e-ae60-4e10-b688-d0cac2a63cb2","published_at":"2008-05-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Colorless is not a color.","oracle_id":"3003e19e-ae60-4e10-b688-d0cac2a63cb2","published_at":"2008-05-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"After the additional beginning phase, the game proceeds to the ending phase (unless something has added even more phases; see below.)","oracle_id":"516101be-be39-4d84-8fee-d8a79930dd0a","published_at":"2020-11-10","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Even if you don't attack with any creatures during combat, you'll still get a postcombat main phase and Sphinx of the Second Sun's ability will still trigger.","oracle_id":"516101be-be39-4d84-8fee-d8a79930dd0a","published_at":"2020-11-10","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If multiple phases are added to the same point in your turn, the most recently created phase happens first. For example, say you control Sphinx of the Second Sun and its ability triggers during your postcombat main phase. Later during that same main phase, another effect gives you an additional combat phase after this main phase. The additional combat will happen first, followed by the additional beginning phase.","oracle_id":"516101be-be39-4d84-8fee-d8a79930dd0a","published_at":"2020-11-10","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If you somehow have more than two main phases in a turn, each main phase other than the first one is a postcombat main phase, and Sphinx of the Second Sun's ability triggers at the beginning of each of them.","oracle_id":"516101be-be39-4d84-8fee-d8a79930dd0a","published_at":"2020-11-10","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"The additional beginning phase all happens during the current turn. Any effects that last \"until your next turn\" or similar won't expire just because you'll go through an additional beginning phase.","oracle_id":"516101be-be39-4d84-8fee-d8a79930dd0a","published_at":"2020-11-10","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"The additional beginning phase will be a lot like your normal beginning phase. During the untap step, permanents will phase in or out as appropriate and you'll untap your tapped permanents. Anything that triggers \"at the beginning of your upkeep\" or similar will trigger during the upkeep step, and you'll eventually draw a card for your draw step.","oracle_id":"516101be-be39-4d84-8fee-d8a79930dd0a","published_at":"2020-11-10","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Magnetic Theft can cause an Equipment one player controls to be attached to a creature another player controls. The controller of the Equipment can pay the equip cost to move the Equipment to a creature they control (but only any time that player could cast a sorcery).","oracle_id":"9b22cc97-003f-4227-acdc-7a0857674b67","published_at":"2004-12-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"This is not modal. If the target changes from an artifact to an enchantment or vice versa, this still destroys it.","oracle_id":"a7e97fa9-4b72-4548-b854-5be5f18a6f1a","published_at":"2004-10-04","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"An effect that changes a permanent's colors overwrites all its old colors unless it specifically says \"in addition to its other colors.\" For example, after Cerulean Wisps resolves, the affected creature will just be blue. It doesn't matter what colors it used to be (even if, for example, it used to be blue and black).","oracle_id":"e699d140-eb13-4f15-aecb-85c76e8b1b14","published_at":"2008-05-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Changing a permanent's color won't change its text. If you turn Wilt-Leaf Liege blue, it will still affect green creatures and white creatures.","oracle_id":"e699d140-eb13-4f15-aecb-85c76e8b1b14","published_at":"2008-05-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Colorless is not a color.","oracle_id":"e699d140-eb13-4f15-aecb-85c76e8b1b14","published_at":"2008-05-01","source":"wotc"}],"schema_version":1,"source":"Scryfall Oracle/rulings subset for offline tests"}
